Proof interpretation
  The rigorous wall is a divisor-lattice statement, not a primality statement.
  Node 3 cannot be replaced by a finite residue certificate: the committed speed
  forces witness denominators beyond every fixed bound.  The useful replacement
  is an effective equidistribution/prime-power-residue lemma for denominators
  just beyond the lcm wall, composed with the finite Node 2 AP/three-gap cap.

